1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,783
This is the last lecture, and it teaches you nothing new.

2
00:00:06,583 --> 00:00:10,061
It's a studio, where you build, you play,

3
00:00:10,511 --> 00:00:13,120
and you write down what happened.

4
00:00:14,920 --> 00:00:19,267
By the end you'll have act one finished and walked,

5
00:00:19,717 --> 00:00:23,196
and the other three acts on a page.

6
00:00:24,396 --> 00:00:26,570
Three sittings, on one save.

7
00:00:28,370 --> 00:00:32,283
In the first, I play evenings one and two,

8
00:00:32,733 --> 00:00:35,776
on the file exactly as it stands.

9
00:00:36,676 --> 00:00:41,024
Then I stop, and I write evenings four and five.

10
00:00:42,824 --> 00:00:44,998
I do that on purpose,

11
00:00:45,448 --> 00:00:48,926
because it's how you'll write the other fifteen:

12
00:00:49,376 --> 00:00:51,550
with a crew already playing.

13
00:00:53,350 --> 00:00:56,828
Then two more sittings to finish the act.

14
00:00:58,028 --> 00:01:02,811
Sitting one is a walk, as fast as I can go.

15
00:01:03,711 --> 00:01:05,450
The levy, a job,

16
00:01:05,900 --> 00:01:07,639
the Wren and home,

17
00:01:08,089 --> 00:01:09,828
the Dunlin and home.

18
00:01:11,628 --> 00:01:13,802
And here's where I stop.

19
00:01:14,702 --> 00:01:17,746
The open step is three of five.

20
00:01:18,646 --> 00:01:21,254
Four and five are still stubs,

21
00:01:21,704 --> 00:01:24,748
and the crew can't see them yet.

22
00:01:26,548 --> 00:01:28,287
I close the game.

23
00:01:29,487 --> 00:01:32,965
Now I write, with a game in progress.

24
00:01:34,765 --> 00:01:39,113
Evening four is one step that goes to the Petrel.

25
00:01:40,013 --> 00:01:42,187
I change where it leads,

26
00:01:42,637 --> 00:01:46,550
and I add an objective and a way home.

27
00:01:48,350 --> 00:01:50,959
Is that safe for the save?

28
00:01:51,859 --> 00:01:54,033
Yes, and I know why.

29
00:01:54,483 --> 00:01:57,091
The crew hasn't finished that step,

30
00:01:57,541 --> 00:02:01,889
so its new line will be read when they do.

31
00:02:02,789 --> 00:02:07,137
And the new steps are ahead of them, not behind.

32
00:02:08,337 --> 00:02:12,685
Evening five is a talk evening, in the Gleaners' yard.

33
00:02:13,585 --> 00:02:15,324
There are two answers,

34
00:02:15,774 --> 00:02:17,948
and either one finishes it.

35
00:02:19,748 --> 00:02:22,357
But this time they're held back.

36
00:02:23,257 --> 00:02:26,300
If learned, the Gleaners broke a boat.

37
00:02:28,100 --> 00:02:32,448
A crew that hails them cold won't see either answer.

38
00:02:33,348 --> 00:02:36,826
They have to ask the right question first.

39
00:02:38,626 --> 00:02:41,235
That's the fact from lecture two,

40
00:02:41,685 --> 00:02:43,424
doing a real job.

41
00:02:45,224 --> 00:02:48,267
And the step's second paragraph says so.

42
00:02:49,167 --> 00:02:52,646
A crew that's stuck reads the Quest Log,

43
00:02:53,096 --> 00:02:55,704
so that's where the hint goes.

44
00:02:56,904 --> 00:03:01,252
And one change to something the crew has already seen.

45
00:03:02,152 --> 00:03:06,500
The step they're on had a placeholder for a title.

46
00:03:07,400 --> 00:03:09,139
I change the title,

47
00:03:09,589 --> 00:03:12,198
and I leave the key alone.

48
00:03:13,998 --> 00:03:17,911
One more step, for act two to stand on.

49
00:03:18,811 --> 00:03:21,854
It stays open when the act ends,

50
00:03:22,304 --> 00:03:24,913
and act two will finish it.

51
00:03:26,713 --> 00:03:29,322
It could be open for weeks,

52
00:03:29,772 --> 00:03:31,946
so it gets a page.

53
00:03:32,846 --> 00:03:37,628
A paragraph, and a short list of what's still out there.

54
00:03:39,428 --> 00:03:42,037
I save, and I run lint.

55
00:03:42,937 --> 00:03:45,980
One warning, and for once it's true.

56
00:03:46,430 --> 00:03:48,604
Nothing sends that signal yet.

57
00:03:50,404 --> 00:03:53,883
If it said a step is never revealed,

58
00:03:54,333 --> 00:03:57,376
I'd stop right here and fix it.

59
00:03:58,576 --> 00:04:02,054
Sitting two, and I don't delete the save.

60
00:04:03,854 --> 00:04:06,898
The open step has its new name.

61
00:04:07,798 --> 00:04:10,841
My words reached a game in progress.

62
00:04:12,641 --> 00:04:16,120
Evening three is the assay office, and home.

63
00:04:17,020 --> 00:04:18,759
Then comes evening four.

64
00:04:19,659 --> 00:04:21,833
I arrive at the Petrel,

65
00:04:22,283 --> 00:04:26,196
and there's the step I wrote an hour ago.

66
00:04:27,096 --> 00:04:30,139
I scan her, and I go home.

67
00:04:31,939 --> 00:04:34,548
Now five of five is waiting.

68
00:04:35,448 --> 00:04:37,622
I close the game again.

69
00:04:38,822 --> 00:04:40,561
And the last sitting.

70
00:04:42,361 --> 00:04:45,404
At the yard, I hail the Gleaners.

71
00:04:46,304 --> 00:04:48,043
There are four answers,

72
00:04:48,493 --> 00:04:51,102
and neither of my new ones.

73
00:04:52,902 --> 00:04:55,946
I ask what became of the boats,

74
00:04:56,396 --> 00:04:58,135
and I hail again.

75
00:04:59,035 --> 00:05:00,774
Now there are six.

76
00:05:02,574 --> 00:05:04,313
I buy the log.

77
00:05:04,763 --> 00:05:06,502
The step is done,

78
00:05:06,952 --> 00:05:09,126
and the act's ending appears.

79
00:05:10,926 --> 00:05:12,665
Home, and it pays.

80
00:05:13,565 --> 00:05:17,043
Every line of the long count is done,

81
00:05:17,493 --> 00:05:20,972
but the one that's waiting for act two.

82
00:05:22,172 --> 00:05:23,911
Now for the page.

83
00:05:24,811 --> 00:05:29,159
Act one's table says in full, all the way down.

84
00:05:30,959 --> 00:05:33,133
I write what I played:

85
00:05:33,583 --> 00:05:38,365
three sittings, with the credits and the open step each time.

86
00:05:40,165 --> 00:05:42,774
And then the other three acts.

87
00:05:43,674 --> 00:05:46,717
One table each, one row an evening.

88
00:05:47,167 --> 00:05:51,515
A title, a place, a style, and how it ends.

89
00:05:53,315 --> 00:05:55,924
I don't write a single record.

90
00:05:56,824 --> 00:05:59,867
There's one win in the whole campaign,

91
00:06:00,317 --> 00:06:02,491
and it's on evening twenty.

92
00:06:03,691 --> 00:06:05,865
Mark yourself against the rubric.

93
00:06:06,765 --> 00:06:10,243
And be honest, the way this page is.

94
00:06:12,043 --> 00:06:15,522
Nobody has sat a crew down to this.

95
00:06:16,422 --> 00:06:19,900
A script did the scanning and the fighting.

96
00:06:20,800 --> 00:06:24,278
Every time on my sheets is a plan.

97
00:06:26,078 --> 00:06:31,296
The last two points on the rubric are the ones that count.

98
00:06:32,196 --> 00:06:35,674
A crew that isn't you plays evening one,

99
00:06:36,124 --> 00:06:38,298
and you watch without helping.

100
00:06:39,498 --> 00:06:41,237
And that's the course.

101
00:06:43,037 --> 00:06:48,254
You have a universe, and a campaign with its first act played.

102
00:06:49,154 --> 00:06:52,198
You have a plan for the rest,

103
00:06:52,648 --> 00:06:57,430
and the habits to write it while a crew is playing.

104
00:06:59,230 --> 00:07:02,709
So there's only one thing left to do.

105
00:07:03,609 --> 00:07:05,783
Go and write evening six.
